---
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
import Documentation from '../layouts/Documentation.astro';
import ChartOptions from '../ChartOptions';
import PublicChartOptions from '../PublicChartOptions';
import references from '../../../../packages/contracts/props.json';
---
<Documentation title="Chart options"><main class="docs-catalogue"><h1>Charts and their options.</h1><p>Use Chart for simple series, AnalyticsChart for analytics rendering, and DashboardChart for an aligned plot with a bounded legend and a stack selector. Supply chronological display-ready data from your data layer.</p><h2>Option applicability</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Applies to</th><th>Interaction</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>referenceLine</td><td>stackedBar, groupedBar, line, multiLine</td><td>Disables split scale; target never contributes to stacked totals.</td></tr><tr><td>cumulative</td><td>stackedBar, groupedBar, stackedArea, line, multiLine</td><td>Running display totals; input remains unchanged.</td></tr><tr><td>partialFrom</td><td>line, multiLine, stackedBar, groupedBar</td><td>Dashed lines or translucent bars; disables split scale.</td></tr><tr><td>highlightIndices</td><td>line / multiLine</td><td>Highlights supplied anomaly indices; detection stays in the data layer.</td></tr><tr><td>splitScale</td><td>stackedBar</td><td>auto, on, off; incompatible with target/partial markers.</td></tr><tr><td>stackedBarLabel</td><td>stackedBar</td><td>value, percent, none.</td></tr><tr><td>valueFormat</td><td>Numeric axes and tooltips</td><td>percent formats supplied ratio values.</td></tr><tr><td>stackOptions</td><td>DashboardChart</td><td>Controlled stackBy/onStackByChange; application supplies the resulting series.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={base+"/components/AnalyticsChart/"}>Complete renderer props and recipe</a> · <a href={base+"/components/DashboardChart/"}>Dashboard composition</a> · <a href={base+"/components/Sparkline/"}>Sparkline</a></p><PublicChartOptions client:only="react"/><ChartOptions client:only="react"/><h2>Custom chart APIs</h2><nav class="docs-index"><a href={`${base}/components/RelationshipPlot/`}>RelationshipPlot</a><a href={`${base}/components/ForecastAdjustmentChart/`}>ForecastAdjustmentChart</a><a href={`${base}/components/ShareBreakdown/`}>ShareBreakdown</a><a href={`${base}/components/WaterfallChart/`}>WaterfallChart</a><a href={`${base}/components/CapacityBreakdown/`}>CapacityBreakdown</a><a href={`${base}/components/RadarComparison/`}>RadarComparison</a><a href={`${base}/components/CumulativeChart/`}>CumulativeChart</a><a href={`${base}/components/DistributionChart/`}>DistributionChart</a></nav><nav class="docs-index" aria-label="Custom chart contracts"><a href={`${base}/components/CapacityBubbleChart/`}>CapacityBubbleChart</a><a href={`${base}/components/ForecastActualChart/`}>ForecastActualChart</a><a href={`${base}/components/AllocationTimeline/`}>AllocationTimeline</a></nav><p>The custom bubble chart accepts positioned bubbles and callbacks, the burndown accepts cumulative values with null for missing actuals, and Gantt accepts display-ready tasks. Their application adapters calculate capacities, financial totals and allocations. <a href={base+"/compatibility.json"}>Download the generated signatures for every custom chart and timeline export.</a></p></main></Documentation>
